{
 "summary": "Checkout failures originate in inventory, not gateway. Inventory logs 'connection pool exhausted' and returns 500 on POST /reserve. Orders turns that into a 502, and gateway turns that into a 502 to clients, all in the same traces. The gateway 1.5.3 deploy at 09:13:13Z came shortly before the errors, but nothing in the evidence ties gateway's change to inventory's pool exhaustion.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory's connection pool is exhausted, so inventory POST /reserve returns 500. That failure propagates as 502s through orders and gateway on checkout. What exhausted the pool (an inventory resource or its backend, or a change in traffic) is not shown in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
   "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
   "ev-2bbdc45c9d49",
   "ev-b07f2f336800",
   "ev-4df59038eeb9"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway was deployed from 1.4.2 to 1.5.3 at 09:13:13Z, about 32s before the first error logs. The timing is close, but no evidence links the gateway change to inventory's pool exhaustion.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17ee17817f45",
    "ev-b07f2f336800"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Failing requests are fast (7-20ms) and p95 latencies stay low in every service, so the pool appears to fail fast rather than causing a timeout cascade.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:13:13Z",
   "event": "Gateway deployed 1.4.2 -> 1.5.3 by ci-pipeline.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17ee17817f45"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:13:45Z",
   "event": "Inventory starts logging 'connection pool exhausted'. Orders logs inventory 500s and gateway logs orders 502s at the same moment (98 each, sharing the same example traces).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-2bbdc45c9d49",
    "ev-b07f2f336800"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:14:12.969000Z",
   "event": "5xx ratio crosses 5% for inventory, orders and gateway at the same time. Inventory and orders peak at 50%, gateway at 36.8%.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T09:15:42Z",
   "event": "Sampled error traces show the chain: inventory POST /reserve 500 -> orders POST /orders 502 -> gateway POST /checkout 502.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway as the origin of the errors is unlikely. Its errors are propagated 502s from orders ('checkout failed: orders returned 502'), and the deepest failing span is inventory's 500.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-b07f2f336800",
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders as the origin is unlikely. It logs that the inventory reservation failed with status 500, and its error ratio matches inventory's.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-2bbdc45c9d49",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A latency or timeout cascade is unlikely. Error traces complete in 7-20ms and no service shows a p95 latency onset.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c",
    "ev-4df59038eeb9",
    "ev-c5447ed2471d",
    "ev-6d5399d5f26e"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "What inventory's connection pool connects to (database or other backend), and that backend's health and saturation metrics. None are in the snapshot.",
  "Whether inventory 3.1.5 or its configuration (pool size) changed recently. Only the gateway deploy is recorded.",
  "Whether gateway 1.5.3 changed the request pattern sent to inventory (retries, more concurrent reservations). Request rates look flat at about 1.5-2 rps, which argues against a load spike.",
  "Inventory connection-pool metrics (active/idle/wait) are not available.",
  "Error ratios before 09:13:13 are not shown separately, so a pre-deploy baseline cannot be confirmed."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Investigate inventory's connection pool and its backend: pool usage, leaked or held connections, and backend availability. Restart inventory or raise the pool size as mitigation if the pool is stuck.",
   "rationale": "Inventory's pool exhaustion is the deepest error in the failing call chain.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Diff gateway 1.4.2 vs 1.5.3 for changes to checkout calls, such as retries or the number of reserve calls. Consider rolling back gateway as a low-cost test if the inventory fix is not quick.",
   "rationale": "The deploy came about 30s before the errors and is a temporal lead, but no causal link is shown.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-17ee17817f45",
    "ev-b07f2f336800"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces de56d9800be16db71b8d60f2d05d39f4 and fe18f4cf5d103fa0162e0bcd0d698bad for inventory spans that touch the pool or a database.",
   "rationale": "These traces would confirm where inside inventory the failure occurs.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-23d4c2b9c411",
    "ev-97ec8dd1752c"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
